+# Incidents brief, August–September 2026
+
+## 11 August: ingest stall and full disk
+
+- **Impact:** about 2.5 hours overnight. Customers saw stale dashboards; no data lost.
+- **Root cause:** one malformed batch jammed ingest, which retried it endlessly; the retry logs then filled the database disk.
+- **Fix:** restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside, then reclaimed disk space (97% → 61%).
+- **Follow-ups:**
+  - Disk alert at 80%: no owner named; open.
+  - Paging escalation (15-minute wait): Elif and Sunil; done, confirmed 30 Sep.
+  - Handbook check for the old wait: Mara; open.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingest: Jonas; open.
+
+## 21 September: API certificate expiry
+
+- **Impact:** 47-minute outage of the public API; nearly every client failed.
+- **Root cause:** the certificate expired; its renewal job had failed silently all month on an outdated token.
+- **Fix:** renewed the certificate and restarted the API.
+- **Follow-ups** (no owners named):
+  - Renewal job alerts on failure: done.
+  - Reminder 14 days before expiry: open.
+  - Alert on days remaining: open.
+  - Expiry check in weekly checklist: open.
+  - Responders log actions as they go: agreed practice.
